    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters August 27th with a primary objective of maximizing stolen base efficiency while navigating a challenging slate of opposing arms. **Corbin Carroll** (75.28) and **Mickey Moniak** (73.09) headline our starts today, both benefiting from favorable matchups against Landen Roupp and Jake Irvin, respectively. **Corbin Carroll** remains the engine of our SB strategy; while his score takes a slight 2% hit due to the opposing backstop\u2019s pop time, his position in the #2 hole and the favorable xERA of 4.34 make him our most potent asset. **Vinnie Pasquantino** (72.92) also grades as a strong play; facing Spencer Arrighetti allows for a significant 14% platoon edge, pushing his total comfortably into the upper-tier of our daily expectations.\n\nThe decision to start **Gabriel Moreno** (60.66) over other bench options was predicated on his projected role in the heart of the order, providing a critical buffer against the 4.34 xERA of Landen Roupp. Conversely, **Austin Riley** (45.13) sits on the razor's edge of our \"marginal\" category. He faced the most significant downward pressure today, hampered by a tough matchup against Yoshinobu Yamamoto (3.49 xERA) and a drop to the #8 spot in the lineup. While **Brice Turang** (50.33) and **Isaac Paredes** (51.52) also posted scores near the 50-point mark, they are active only due to a lack of superior alternatives on a light day. **Brice Turang** remains a tactical risk due to his high SB-suppression matchup against Sean Manaea, which accounts for a 4% penalty to his score.\n\nWe are navigating significant depth issues, as **Josh Naylor** and **Seiya Suzuki** are sidelined by team off-days, while **James Wood** and **Trevor Story** remain on the IL, limiting our ability to pivot when matchups turn sour. We are keeping a close eye on **Jose Caballero** (55.53), who is currently our most volatile start; his projected #9 spot and a unfavorable platoon dynamic against Hayden Wesneski nearly pushed him to the bench. For tomorrow\u2019s outlook, we are monitoring the development of prospects like **Dalton Rushing**, **Travis Bazzana**, and **Henry Bolte**, alongside bench depth pieces **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Max Muncy**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Griffin Conine**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Cole Young**, as we may need to rotate fresh legs into the lineup if today's marginal starts fail to deliver on base-path productivity.",
